<div class="dt-shop">
  <h2>Enable an NPC merchant</h2>
  <p>Only GMs can open or edit the NPC sheet. Players browse public stock through the separate Shop UI.</p>
  <label>NPC <select name="npc" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>{{#each npcs}}<option value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{name}}{{#if enabled}} (enabled){{/if}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>
  <label>Availability <select name="availability"><option value="open">Open</option><option value="closed">Closed</option>
    <option value="busy">Busy</option><option value="travelling">Travelling</option><option value="sleeping">Sleeping</option></select></label>
  <button type="button" data-action="enable" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Enable / update linked tokens</button>
  <p role="status">{{message}}</p>
  <p>Only Items copied from Devil's Table or manually given an approved public description and price appear in player stock.</p>
  <hr>
  <h3>Trade settings</h3>
  <button type="button" data-action="loadTerms">Load selected merchant settings</button>
  <label><input type="checkbox" name="infinite" {{#if infinite}}checked{{/if}}>Infinite merchant funds (native balance unchanged)</label>
  <label><input type="checkbox" name="exactChange" {{#if terms.exactChange}}checked{{/if}}>Require available denominations (finite wallets)</label>
  <label>Merchant buys at multiplier <input name="buyModifier" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="0.01" value="{{terms.buyModifier}}"></label>
  <label>Merchant sells at multiplier <input name="sellModifier" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="0.01" value="{{terms.sellModifier}}"></label>
  <button type="button" data-action="saveTerms">Save trade settings</button>
  <button type="button" data-action="recover">Check / recover interrupted trade</button>
  <p>Receipts are in the private Devil's Table — Private Transactions compendium. Recovery restores an interrupted trade only when the saved changes still match; conflicting edits require manual GM reconciliation.</p>
  <hr>
  <h3>Optional starting stock</h3>
  <p>Build the Item compendium and Stock RollTables first. Roll a preview, then add the chosen assortment with its weighted quantities. Existing inventory and prices are preserved.</p>
  {{#if stockError}}<p role="alert">{{stockError}}</p>{{/if}}
  <label>Stock profile <select name="profile" {{#if stockBlocked}}disabled{{/if}}>{{#each profiles}}<option value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{name}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>
  <button type="button" data-action="previewStock" {{#if stockBlocked}}disabled{{/if}}>Roll stock preview</button>
  {{#if preview}}
    <h3>{{previewMerchant}} — {{preview.profileName}}</h3>
    <ul class="dt-report">{{#each preview.items}}<li>{{#if skip}}Keep existing: {{else}}Add {{quantity}} × {{/if}}{{name}} — {{price.value}} {{price.denomination}} per {{saleUnit}}</li>{{/each}}</ul>
    <button type="button" data-action="addStock" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Add previewed stock to {{previewMerchant}}</button>
  {{/if}}
</div>
